#
# Conformance case: contracts/belnap-counterfactual-revision-unsupported
# AC (#767 Gap 2 / #766 ME1): a ReasoningContract that pairs the Belnap bilattice
# truth algebra (logic:BelnapBilattice) with counterfactual entrenchment revision
# (logic:EntrenchmentRevision) is a FORBIDDEN facet combination
# (RuleNoParaconsistentCounterfactualRevision): the closest-world selection that
# generates the counterfactual states is not defined over gappy or glutty
# valuations. The compile MUST emit an UNSUPPORTED_CONTRACT Severity::Error and the
# harness MUST short-circuit before evaluating — the "unsupported is a hard stop"
# guarantee, pinned at the corpus level (profile.json declares
# "expect_unsupported": true).
#
# The pre-existing paraconsistent-counterfactual-revision case exercises this rule
# via its admissibleValuation (gap/glut) LHS branch; this case pins the SECOND LHS
# branch — the truth-algebra (logic:BelnapBilattice) trigger — so both alternative
# conditions of the rule are covered at the corpus level.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/contracts/belnap-counterfactual-revision/> .

ex:UnsupportedContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:truthAlgebra logic:BelnapBilattice ;
    logic:revision logic:EntrenchmentRevision .
